-### Direct Light Contribution Estimation
-- **Step:** Calculate direct light contribution for each voxel: 1. Retrieve local opacity $\alpha_l(s_0)$ from local piecewise integration. 2. Interpolate global opacity $\alpha_g(s_1)$ from the SVR for the segment from $s_1$ to the light source. 3. Apply Eq. 8 [S4].
-- **Formula:** $I_d(s_0) = I_0 \cdot (1 - \alpha_g(s_1)) \cdot (1 - \alpha_l(s_0))$, where $I_d(s_0)$ is direct light intensity at $s_0$, $I_0$ is source intensity, $\alpha_g(s_1)$ is global opacity from $s_1$ to light, and $\alpha_l(s_0)$ is local opacity at $s_0$ [S4].
-- **Parameter:** Source Intensity ($I_0$): A user-defined parameter representing the light source intensity [S4].
-- **Pitfall:** Local Occlusion Accuracy: Using only $\alpha_g$ for the entire ray reduces quality. Using local $\alpha_l(s_0)$ for the first segment ensures highest resolution for local occlusion [S4].
